=head1 NAME

t/unit/mason/text/sentences_breeders_toolbox_trial_4.t - breeders_toolbox/trial templates, part 4 of 5: sentences appear in the user's language

=head1 DESCRIPTION

Renders components with SGN::Test::MasonText in English and with a test
translation. Components needing real data are compiled only.

=cut

use strict;
use warnings;
use utf8;

use lib 't/lib';
use Test::More;
use SGN::Test::MasonText qw( page_sentences_ok component_compiles_ok );

page_sentences_ok(
    '/breeders_toolbox/trial/trial_status.mas',
    'Has Plots{break}And Plants',
);

page_sentences_ok(
    '/breeders_toolbox/trial/trial_upload_dialogs.mas',
    'A field trial represents plots in the field where each plot has a globally unique {plot_name}, a sequential {plot_number} that is unique in the trial (e.g. 101, 102, 103 for three separate plots), and an {accession_name} representing the genotype being tested in that plot. In cases where a cross/family is being evaluated (e.g. F1 hybrid, backcrossing), a {cross_unique_id} or a {family_name} can be used instead of an {accession_name_plain}. Each plot can belong to different blocks ({block_number}) and reps ({rep_number}) depending on the experimental design you are using (e.g. complete block vs augmented design). Each plot can have a {row_number} and {col_number} indicating the relative position of the plot in the field.',
    'You can provide the specific {seedlot_name} planted in each plot, along with the number of seeds ({num_seed_per_plot}) and/or the weight (g) of seed ({weight_gram_seed_per_plot}) that were used. For plots of family name stock type, seedlots of cross members in the family can be used.',
    'Experimental treatments are handled in much the same way as phenotypes, and can be uploaded from the trial detail page after trial creation. They may also be included as additional columns in a trial upload, formatted as {experimental_treatment_experiment_treatment_0000001}',
    'If the stocks that are being evaluated in any trial are crosses or family names, {trial_stock_type} column is required and indicates as {cross} or {family_name}. All rows for the same trial must have the same trial stock type.',
    'Plots can be named manually, automatically by the database, or in accordance with a plot naming template. Visit the {em}Autogenerated Name Metadata{end_em} section of your breeding program page to create plot name templates.',
    '{plot_name} (must be unique across entire database. If not provided in the file, it will be automatically generated as {trial_name_plot_plot_number}, or according to a plot name template if specified.)',
);

page_sentences_ok(
    '/breeders_toolbox/trial/update_experimental_design_type.mas',
    'Current Experimental Design type: {design}',
);

component_compiles_ok('/breeders_toolbox/trial/update_trial_status_dialog.mas');

done_testing;
